---
description: Prefer discriminated unions over parallel booleans in the web app
globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Client state unions

Encode modes as one discriminated union. Do not keep independent flags or optionals that can disagree.

```ts
// BAD — feed + tag can both look "on"
const feed = !tag && searchParams.get("feed") === "following";

// GOOD
type FeedMode =
  | { kind: "global" }
  | { kind: "following" }
  | { kind: "tag"; tag: string };
```

Same idea for editor create vs edit, list loading/error/success, auth snapshot (`authenticated` implies `user`), and profile article tabs.

Destructure `useQuery` (and similar) at the call site. Do not wrap it in a custom hook unless the user asks.

Prefer one small modeling win. Avoid large extract or type-hygiene tours that only move code.
